From 1a92a6f86fefb402f8d8c23d389b46c04a028fb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:54:46 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] rocket RK3576: derive the first conv's padding instead of
 hardcoding it

fill_regcmd_firstconv wrote 0x1080 = 0x00000101, pad_left 1 and pad_top 1,
which is symmetric padding of one. That is what a torch conv with padding=1
asks for and what the capture this function was written from contained.
MobileNet's conv0 is tflite SAME padding, which for 224 to 112 at stride 2 with
a 3x3 kernel needs ONE pad in total: pad_top and pad_left are 0, pad_bottom and
pad_right are 1, which is 0x01010000, the opposite corner.

Measured with an impulse first conv, one live tap per output channel: the
hardware decodes to the input shifted one pixel up and to the left of where the
CPU puts it, on all 32 channels at correlation 1.000. Every value is then wrong
because of where it reads rather than what it computes, which is why sweeping
the requant moved the output everywhere without making one channel correct.

The generic path has derived this register since the round that established
what it was; the first conv kept the literal. ROCKET_FC_PAD forces a value and
0x00000101 restores the old one as a control.

Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
index 82060c7..9def453 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
@@ -157,7 +157,30 @@ fill_first_regcmd_rk3576_firstconv(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
    R_CNA(0x1074, 0x00000000);
    R_CNA(0x1078, 0x002900df);
    R_CNA(0x107c, 0x00000002);
-   R_CNA(0x1080, 0x00000101);
+   /*
+    * The PADDING register, derived rather than hardcoded.
+    *
+    * 0x00000101 is pad_left = 1 and pad_top = 1, which is symmetric padding of
+    * one on every side. That is what a torch conv with padding=1 asks for, and
+    * it is what the capture this function was written from contained. tflite
+    * SAME padding on MobileNet's conv0 is NOT symmetric: 224 to 112 at stride 2
+    * with a 3x3 kernel needs one pad in total, so pad_top and pad_left are 0
+    * and pad_bottom and pad_right are 1, which is 0x01010000, the opposite
+    * corner.
+    *
+    * Measured: an impulse first conv, one live tap per output channel, decodes
+    * on hardware to exactly the input shifted one pixel UP AND LEFT of where
+    * the CPU puts it, on all 32 channels at correlation 1.000. Every value is
+    * then wrong and no requant can rescue it, which is what the sweep in round
+    * 80 found.
+    *
+    * The generic path has derived this since the round that found CNA 0x1080
+    * was a padding register at all; the first conv kept the literal.
+    * ROCKET_FC_PAD forces a value, and 0x00000101 restores the old one.
+    */
+   R_CNA(0x1080, rkt_env_u32("ROCKET_FC_PAD",
+                             (task->pad_right << 24) | (task->pad_bottom << 16) |
+                             (task->pad_left << 8) | task->pad_top));
    R_CNA(0x1084, 0x00808080);
    R_CNA(0x1088, feature_addr); /* input feature base addr */
    R_CNA(0x108c, 0x000f000f);
-- 
